55
00:03:27,659 --> 00:03:32,460
And so basically what's happening is these memories are managed by IDs.

56
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:39,259
And so when we call to this tool, we can pass in the ID of a memory, the action we want

57
00:03:39,259 --> 00:03:43,860
to take on it, whether we should update it or create it or delete it.

58
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:48,900
And then the content of that memory as well.

59
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:52,980
If we look at the search memory tool, we can see that it's called search memory.

60
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:56,340
